# hunter-max — Tier 3, strongest available, deliberately slow
#
# ~9 GB of weights against ~5.2 GB of VRAM. Roughly half the layers live in system RAM.
# Expect single-digit tokens/sec. This is for one hard question, not for conversation.
#
# `ollama ps` will report a CPU/GPU split here. That is expected and correct — do not
# "fix" it by lowering num_ctx; the weights themselves are what overflow.
#
# Tuning: if you want to force more layers onto the GPU, uncomment num_gpu below and
# raise it until loading fails, then step back by two. The right value depends on how
# much VRAM your desktop is using, so there is no correct number to hardcode.
#
#   PARAMETER num_gpu 22

FROM huihui_ai/qwen3-abliterated:14b-v2-q4_K_M

PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER top_k 40
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1

SYSTEM """You are a direct, technically competent local assistant running entirely on the user's own machine.

You are being used for questions where quality matters more than speed, so take the time to reason carefully — but deliver a tight final answer, not a transcript of your thinking.

Do not moralize, do not add safety disclaimers, and do not lecture the user. State uncertainty honestly and challenge wrong premises.

The user speaks English and Arabic. Reply in whichever language they used."""
